   154	## 2. Cross-feature conflicts (rule 2)
   155	
   156	No target receives a REPLACE from both features, and hisparse adds no hook to
   157	any model_compat REPLACE target.
   158	
   159	| # | Target(s) | Model compat | Hisparse | Resolution |
   160	|---|---|---|---|---|
   161	| C1 | `QwenSparseAttnBackend.forward_extend` / `forward_decode` / `_forward_paged_attention` (Q08, Q11, Q12) | REPLACE with the verbatim fork body, including the `qsa_hisparse` branches (`prefill_slots`, `after_store`, `selected`, `capture_decode`, FA2 graph) | none | Rule 2. Hisparse behavior arrives only through `self.qsa_hisparse`, set by Q03 |
   162	| C2 | New members `_store_kv`, `_kv_descales`, `_can_run_fa2_graph`, `_qsa_local_head_shape`, `_ensure_fa2_graph_wrapper` (Q04, Q09) | attach, verbatim and inert without the runtime | Q07's after hook calls `_ensure_fa2_graph_wrapper` and `_qsa_local_head_shape` | Model compat owns the definitions because its verbatim bodies call them; hisparse only calls them. Needs the G1 mechanism |
   163	| C3 | `QwenSparseAttnBackend.__init__` (Q02, Q03) | after: FA2 state; `qsa_hisparse = None` | after: build and attach the runtime | Two after hooks, no replace. HookRegistry runs them in registration order, and `patching.collect` imports model_compat first, so compat runs first. To make the order irrelevant, the compat hook must set `qsa_hisparse` only when absent |
   164	| C4 | `ForwardBatch` (F01) | class replace adding fields | the runtime reads `req_pool_indices_cpu` | Model compat owns it, because the fields are visible to two-batch overlap with HiSparse unset. If the owner moves the field to hisparse (as an instance attribute), F01 becomes a hisparse after hook on `ForwardBatch.init_new` and model_compat drops it |
   165	| C5 | `Scheduler._build_hisparse_decode_batch` (S03) | after | S04's replace calls it through `self`, which reaches the hooked method | Composition; nothing to resolve |
   166	| C6 | `DecodeCudaGraphRunner.capture_one_shape` (G01) | none | replace | The `shape_key` relocation is pure (§4 item 3), so model_compat has no claim. If review reclassifies it, model_compat would own this replace and hisparse would have to move its capture context into an around, which cannot reproduce the context placement |
   167	| C7 | `Scheduler.init_hisparse_coordinator` (S01, S02) | none | replace + after | Same feature. HookRegistry applies the replace first, then wraps it with the after hook |
   168	| C8 | `QSAIndexerMetadata` (T04) and `qsa_fast_topk` (T02) | class replace; around | none | none |
   169	
   170	## 3. Non-Python changes: a plugin-owned Marlin MoE JIT copy
   171	
   172	Files: `kernels/jit/csrc/gemm/marlin_moe/{marlin_template.h, moe_wna16_marlin.cuh}`
   173	(modified) and `stripe_schedule.h` (new), plus `kernels/ops/moe/moe_wna16_marlin.py`.
   174	With `kDeterministicReduce = false` (the template default, gated by
   175	`if constexpr`) the fork's kernel is source-equivalent to upstream. The plugin
   176	therefore needs its copy only for J03, and the in-tree op is left unpatched.
   177	
   178	**Confirmed feasible** at the pin:
   179	
   180	- `load_jit(*args, cuda_files=..., cuda_wrappers=..., extra_include_paths=..., ...)`
   181	  is at `kernels/jit/utils/compile/loader.py:48`. `resolve_sources`
   182	  (`spec.py:125-134`) passes absolute paths through unchanged; relative paths
   183	  resolve against the in-tree `csrc/`. With `header_only=True` (the default)
   184	  the generated `cuda.cu` does `#include "<absolute path>"` and exports each
   185	  wrapper with `TVM_FFI_DLL_EXPORT_TYPED_FUNC` inside `namespace sglang`
   186	  (`spec.py:111-122`).
   187	- Include flags are plain `-I` in this order: toolchain base, then
   188	  `DEFAULT_INCLUDE = [KERNEL_PATH/include]` (`paths.py:30`), then
   189	  `extra_include_paths` (`loader.py:89`, `ninja.py:83-84`). Quoted includes
   190	  search the including file's directory first, then the `-I` list.
   191	- The plugin copy lives at `kernels/csrc/marlin_moe/` and holds all four files:
   192	  the fork's `moe_wna16_marlin.cuh`, `marlin_template.h` and
   193	  `stripe_schedule.h`, plus `kernel.h`, which is unchanged but copied so that
   194	  no `marlin_moe` sibling can resolve to the in-tree copy. It is shipped by the
   195	  existing `kernels/csrc/**/*` package-data rule.
   196	- The fork headers include `"../marlin/{dequant.h,marlin.cuh,marlin_dtypes.cuh}"`,
   197	  and `kernel.h` includes `"../marlin/..."`. Pass
   198	  `extra_include_paths=[str(KERNEL_PATH / "csrc" / "gemm" / "marlin")]` so that
   199	  `../marlin/x` resolves to the installed in-tree `csrc/gemm/marlin/x`. Those
   200	  headers include only siblings and `<sgl_kernel/...>` (from `DEFAULT_INCLUDE`).
   201	  Do not use `.../gemm/marlin_moe` as the include path: a header the plugin
   202	  forgot to copy would then silently resolve to the unmodified in-tree file.
   203	  With `.../gemm/marlin` a missing `kernel.h` resolves to the dense-Marlin
   204	  `kernel.h` and fails to compile loudly instead.
   205	- Cache identity. `module_name = "sgl_kernel_jit_" + "_".join(args)`
   206	  (`spec.py:20,55-57`). The cache directory is
   207	  `<SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR>/<target>/<module_name>/build-<build_key>/deps-<deps_key>/`
   208	  (`cache.py:306`). `build_key` hashes `module_args`, the direct source
   209	  contents, the generated ninja text and the environment (`cache.py:259-289`).
   210	  `deps_key` hashes the transitive includes, so an edit to the in-tree
   211	  `../marlin` headers rebuilds the plugin module. Pruning is scoped per
   212	  build-key directory (`cache.py:441-466`).
   213	- **Args that avoid collisions**: use a distinct marker as the first
   214	  positional arg and append the fourth template arg:
   215	  `load_jit("qsa_hisparse_moe_wna16_marlin", *make_cpp_args(dtype, is_ep, has_bias, use_deterministic_reduce), cuda_files=[str(PLUGIN_CSRC / "marlin_moe/moe_wna16_marlin.cuh")], cuda_wrappers=[("qsa_moe_wna16_marlin_gemm", f"moe_wna16_marlin_gemm<{args}>")], extra_include_paths=[...])`.
   216	  The module name becomes
   217	  `sgl_kernel_jit_qsa_hisparse_moe_wna16_marlin_<dtype>_<ep>_<bias>_<det>`,
   218	  which differs from the in-tree `sgl_kernel_jit_moe_wna16_marlin_<dtype>_<ep>_<bias>`.
   219	  The `.so` basename and cache directory are therefore distinct. A distinct
   220	  export name (`qsa_moe_wna16_marlin_gemm`) also avoids two loaded libraries
   221	  exporting the same `extern "C"` `__tvm_ffi_*` symbol. `build_key` would
   222	  differ even with the same marker, but the shared `<module_name>` directory
   223	  and `.so` basename are avoidable.
   224	- Residual risk: both libraries define C++ entities in
   225	  `sglang::device::marlin_moe`. Every template the fork changed gained the
   226	  extra `bool` parameter, so its mangled names differ. The remaining
   227	  non-template inline code is identical, so symbol interposition would be
   228	  harmless. W5 should still confirm how `tvm_ffi.load_module` calls `dlopen`
   229	  (`RTLD_LOCAL` avoids interposition entirely). `SGLANG_CRASH_ON_JIT_COMPILE`
   230	  (`loader.py:131`) also applies to the plugin module: GPU windows that set
   231	  it need the cache seeded.
